{
  "_comment": [
    "Venue -> research group, the classification behind any grouped view of the",
    "publications. Derived from Web of Science subject categories and rolled up:",
    "'Information Science' and 'Medical Informatics' are WoS category names (the",
    "first shortened from 'Information Science & Library Science'); 'Computer",
    "Science' merges the qualified WoS categories, which are always split as",
    "'Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence' and so on; 'Health & Society'",
    "rolls up Psychology Social, Psychiatry, Psychology Multidisciplinary, Public",
    "Health, Criminology and Sociology, none of which holds more than three papers.",
    "",
    "Conference venues carry no WoS journal category at all — they are indexed in",
    "CPCI — so those are placed by field: ISSI to Information Science, IEEE ICHI",
    "to Medical Informatics, the rest to Computer Science.",
    "",
    "Keyed by venue because the venue decides the group; a new paper in a known",
    "journal classifies itself. Papers whose venue is missing here are reported by",
    "scripts/check-groups.mjs rather than silently dropped."
  ],

